      "structuredContent": {
        "issue": {
          "url": "https://github.com/iamcxa/kc-claude-plugins/issues/815",
          "title": "kc-dev-flow-2: six FO-record rules no script refuses (subspace-relay observer and learn runs, 2026-11-09)",
          "issue_number": 815,
          "body": "Six kc-dev-flow-2 0.35.0 gaps surfaced by observer and learn runs on four subspace-relay tasks (2026-11-09: theme-switch-keeps-draft, room-result-skips-legacy-retraction, signed-in-job-split, pair-pages-favicon). Each is a rule stated in the workflow README or a stage skill that no script refuses, or a script that contradicts its own rule. Not covered by #684.\n\n1. **`gate record` accepts a reason that does not quote the bound question.** `decision_ledger.quotes_bound_question` exists, and every observer flagged it (11 of 12 gates across the four tasks recorded the FO's chat paraphrase, not `answering 「<bound question>」`). Nothing refuses at `gate record` time, so the mismatch is found only after archive. Candidate home: `spacedock gate record` or a pre-record check in `delivery_gate.py`.\n2. **Merge guard archives a task with no committed observer report when `learn` is listed.** README Delivery authority: \"Where `learn` is listed, the sentinel waits for a committed observer report.\" Three tasks were sentinel-recorded and archived without `observer.md`; `observer_check.py` caught it only because the FO ran it by hand on the fourth. Candidate: `merge guard` refuses, or `status --set pr=pr-merge:N` refuses, while `observer_check.py` would print a `next:`.\n3. **No refusal when a merge ask has no `merge/ask-N.json`.** README: \"Before merging or asking, FO runs `delivery_gate.py check`.\" Three of four tasks have no ask record; `merge_audit.py` reports it afterwards as `no ask record:`. Same candidate home as item 2.\n4. **`design_surfaces.py` built-screen check accepts exactly one `preview:` path**, while design-director pass 2a reviews several screenshots and validation needs several sizes. The FO had to narrow the saved report's `preview:` line to one file and keep the reviewed list in a comment (subspace-relay state, `theme-switch-keeps-draft/design/validation-1.yaml`). Candidate: accept a list, each path inside the task folder.\n5. **`dispatch_records.py --coverage` errors on an archived task directory** (observers of two tasks could not run it), so per-stage coverage is unchecked after archive.\n6. **Captain-steps record path disagrees between README and script.** README Captain steps: \"records it in `<task>/captain-steps/<N>.md`\"; `delivery_gate.py` accepts a single `review/captain-steps.md` named on the summary's `Captain steps:` line, which is what every relay task uses. One of them should change.\n\nEvidence: the four observer reports are committed in subspace-relay `spacedock-state/dev2` at `_archive/<task>/observer.md`; the learn jobs (all no-change) are 5e9bc181, b0886821, 2f7f8161, c3f50625 in that repo's local learning store.\n\nFiled at the Captain's request (「同意跑審查，且也同意回報問題」, 2026-11-09).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
